title Tool execution / observed Runtime HTTP path
start
:Completed AssistantMessage contains ToolCalls;
:AgentLoop.resolveToolCallsSafe()\nMatch exact names against this Session's tools;
if (All requested names known?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Create error results for unknown names;\nkeep known calls for normal execution;
endif
:ToolExecutionPipeline.executePlanned()\nAdjacent PARALLEL calls form a batch;\nSEQUENTIAL calls separate batches;
note right
Unknown results are merged back later.
Cancellation aborts the pipeline;
it is not a normal error result.
end note
while (More known calls?) is (yes)
  :Select call / parallel batch;\ncheck cancellation;
  if (Tool JSON Schema valid?) then (yes)
    :beforeToolCall hook\nRuntimeActiveExecution;
    if (Allowed or interaction accepted?) then (yes)
      :ToolExecutionStartEvent;
      :AgentTool.execute()\nLocal read / Mate / Agent / Cron /\nPlan / Question / Todo;
      :Normalize return value;\nordinary exception becomes error result;
      :afterToolCall hook;\nToolExecutionEndEvent;
    else (denied or hook error)
      :Create ToolResultMessage(isError=true)\nwithout executing the tool;
    endif
  else (no)
    :Create ToolResultMessage(isError=true)\nwithout before hook or execution;
  endif
endwhile (no)
:AgentLoop merges known / unknown results\nin original ToolCall order;
:Append ToolResultMessages to context;\nemit TurnEndEvent;
:RuntimeEventProjector persists tool results\nand emits committed public events;
:AgentLoop starts next model turn;
stop
legend bottom
  CallMateTool permission: ALLOW / DENY / ASK.
  ASK waits for user.tool_confirmation before execution.
  ExitPlanMode and AskUserQuestion use separate interaction ports.
endlegend
@enduml

