title One Explicit Skill Command - Historical Implementation
participant Caller
participant "Skill command" as Skill
participant "Message admission" as Admission
participant "Session preparation" as Prep
database "Runtime persistence" as DB
participant "Agent execution" as Run
Caller -> Skill : Submit explicit Skill command
Skill -> Admission : Original invocation and expansion callback
Admission -> Admission : Lock Session; require idle and reconcile model
Admission -> Prep : Restore context and prepare execution
Prep -> Skill : Expand against actual trusted runtime
Skill --> Prep : Validated Skill body and arguments
Prep --> Admission : Prepared execution and expanded input
Admission -> DB : Commit acceptance and execution identity
DB --> Admission : Accepted root
Admission -> Admission : Queue public receipt
Admission -> Run : Start shared model and tool loop
Admission --> Caller : Existing response stream
note over Admission,DB
  Internal context stores expansion; public receipt stores invocation.
  Preparation failure never starts execution.
end note
@enduml

